<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWrecks.xml                    UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S6 "burning-shallows wreck salvage"
  (scald_kit_spec.md §S6: "RUT_ScaldWreck* building defs (2-3 silhouettes,
  art pass) scattered at map-gen in shallow scald water ... Salvage is
  vanilla deconstruct/smash yields").

  ===========================================================================
  FAMILY PARENTS — SALVAGE_WRECKAGE_EVERYWHERE_1 slice 2, 2026-10-06
  ===========================================================================
  The three defs below are children of the shared wreck families in
  mandrake.rm.wreckage (src/RimMandrake/Wreckage/Defs/ThingDefs_Buildings/
  RM_WreckFamilies.xml): Hull -> RM_WreckFamily_Hull, Tank ->
  RM_WreckFamily_Tank, Frame -> RM_WreckFamily_Frame. The families sit on
  Core's ShipChunkBase (static, non-claimable, always deconstructible, no
  rot, corpse or spawner: S6's "cooked clean" structurally) and carry the
  footprint, Walkable affordance, base costList, killedLeavings and the
  RM_CompSalvageLoot tier. Each child here carries only what the Scald did
  to it: label, description, texPath, its art's measured shadow box, and
  the RM_WreckWeathering_Cooked row (yieldFactor 0.75 becomes the
  deconstruct fraction at resolve time, the same 0.75 these defs shipped
  with). Same defNames, same yields, same art: nothing placed changes.
  The RUT_ -> RM_ rename (design §5 tier defect) is a later slice.

  🔴 THREE SILHOUETTES, NOT THREE MECHANICS. Per the spec's own "(2-3
  silhouettes, art pass)" — distinct shapes for scatter variety, all
  carrying the identical salvage mechanism: vanilla costList on
  deconstruct, killedLeavings slag when smashed, PLUS (SALVAGE_WRECKAGE_
  EVERYWHERE_1, 2026-10-06) the shared RM_CompSalvageLoot from
  mandrake.rm.wreckage, which adds a tiered loot roll on careful
  deconstruction only — hull = Hull tier, tank = Tank tier, frame = Scrap
  tier (design/RimMandrake/salvage_wreckage_everywhere_design_2026-10-02.md
  §3c; the Scald's "Hull/Tank tiers, no sealed" row in §4). That comp is
  the "RUT_ScaldSalvage" loot the scald kit spec left open.

  Values (now on the family parents) are INVENTED, stated plainly: sized
  down from ShipChunk_Mech's 40 Steel/15 GravlitePanel (a fresh mechanoid
  chunk); the Cooked weathering's 0.75 is the corrosion. No uranium/component on any of the three: this is hull
  and tankage, not the caskets JawaGroundHulk already owns.

  ⚠️ Ban 6 (no vanilla-Earth flora/fauna) and Ban 2 (no burn-immunity def)
  both hold structurally: nothing here grants terrain immunity or spawns
  life. The burn-per-tick cost of standing in the shallows to deconstruct
  these is paid by the terrain itself (RUT_ScaldWaterShallow's own
  burnDamage/burnIntervalTicks), never waived — S6's own "the price is
  posted in burns per trip" line is the shipped terrain, unchanged.

  🔴 TERRAIN AFFORDANCE: BuildingBase's default Light fails on every
  RUT_ScaldWater*Shallow terrain (WaterShallowBase carries ShallowWater/
  WaterproofConduitable/Bridgeable/Walkable, no Light); RM_WreckFamilyBase
  sets Walkable for every family, so these inherit it.

  Art: SCALD_ART_UPGRADE_WAVE_1, wired 2026-09-26 — THREE Graphic_Random
  variants each (_A/_B/_C, 512px), from the already-finished artpipe renders
  scald2_wreck{hull,tank,frame}_{a,b,c}; they replace the single 256px
  scald_wreck*_v1 sprite each def used to carry. The frame's own three
  variants carry the pawn-scale visible seat the owner asked for. Shadow
  volumes below are RE-CALIBRATED on the new art (the old numbers were
  measured on the retired 256px _A sprites): same ShipChunk-derived
  ~0.70x/0.63x ratio, now applied to the MEAN alpha-bbox fraction across all
  three variants, because shadowData is per-def and one box must serve
  three silhouettes.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_WreckFamily_Hull">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckHull</defName>
    <label>scalded hull section</label>
    <description>A broken length of hull plate, cooked in the shallows until the paint is gone and the seams have given. What the pan swallowed and gave back. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckHull</texPath>
      <!-- Owner review 2026-09-25 (SCALD_REVIEW walk): inherited ShipChunk's
           generic (1.39,0.5,1.25) box read as a flat dark box, not the
           sprite. Calibrated against ShipChunk's own art-to-shadow ratio
           (its sprite fills ~97-100% of its canvas for a (1.39,0.5,1.25)
           shadow on drawSize 2 -> ~0.70x width, ~0.63x height of the sprite
           bbox). MEASURED 2026-09-26 across all three 512px variants
           (_A/_B/_C), mean alpha bbox 93.5% x 87.0% — wide and flat, lying
           wreckage: 0.70*0.935*2=1.31, 0.63*0.870*2=1.10. One box must
           serve three silhouettes, so the mean is the honest input. -->
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(1.31,0.5,1.10)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Wreckage.RM_WreckWeathering">
        <weathering>RM_WreckWeathering_Cooked</weathering>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_WreckFamily_Tank">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckTank</defName>
    <label>scalded tank wreck</label>
    <description>A ruptured pressure tank, half sunk and scoured smooth by the boil. Whatever it once held is long gone; the shell is still worth the walk. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckTank</texPath>
      <!-- Same fix as RUT_ScaldWreckHull, own measurement (mean of _A/_B/_C,
           2026-09-26): 96.4% x 84.3% bbox -> 0.70*0.964*2=1.35,
           0.63*0.843*2=1.06. -->
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(1.35,0.5,1.06)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Wreckage.RM_WreckWeathering">
        <weathering>RM_WreckWeathering_Cooked</weathering>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_WreckFamily_Frame">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldWreckFrame</defName>
    <label>scalded frame wreck</label>
    <description>A stripped strut and frame section, all its skin burned or boiled away, standing bare in the shallows like a rib cage. Deconstruct it for valuable resources — the water charges per trip standing in it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ruins/RUT_ScaldWreckFrame</texPath>
      <!-- Same fix, own measurement (mean of _A/_B/_C, 2026-09-26): 96.5%
           x 90.6% bbox, nearly square — an upright rib-cage frame rather
           than lying wreckage, so this one still gets the tallest shadow of
           the three: 0.70*0.965*2=1.35, 0.63*0.906*2=1.14. -->
      <shadowData>
        <volume>(1.35,0.5,1.14)</volume>
      </shadowData>
    </graphicData>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Wreckage.RM_WreckWeathering">
        <weathering>RM_WreckWeathering_Cooked</weathering>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
